// @run
// @log 1
// @log 1
// @log 2
// THIS FILE USED TO BE A FENCE. It was `run/memory-size-declared-not-lowered.vl`,
// an `@emit-error call to unknown function` pinning that `__memory_size__` was
// declared by the checker and lowered by nothing — "so a program cannot ask how
// big linear memory is. With `__memory_grow__` equally unlowered, the one page
// the memory section hardcodes is the entire budget a program can ever address."
//
// S4 lowered both. The fence became false, so it is kept here as the positive
// pin it turned into, under a name that says what it now asserts:
//
//   __memory_size__()  → 1   the current size, in 64 KiB pages
//   __memory_grow__(1) → 1   the size BEFORE the growth (the spec's return value)
//   __memory_size__()  → 2
//
// The fuller semantics — the -1 failure return, growth past the old ceiling,
// zeroed new pages — are in the sibling files here.
print(__memory_size__())
print(__memory_grow__(1))
print(__memory_size__())
